# The Delve's sounds and music for its browser bundle (crates/web/build.sh).
# Each line: a name prefix ("-" for none), then a folder, from this file's
# own folder; every file in it goes in as <prefix><file>. The game's lines
# name them so: `sfx hit`, `sfx knights-a_cheer_1`, `music music-crypt`.
# The shell fetches each the first time it is asked for: none of them is
# part of the first load.
#
# A third word `beside` keeps that folder out of the `angel` binary: the
# binary's host reads it from disk when it opens its door (the package
# carries the folder beside the binary), and serves what it finds there.
# crates/web/build.sh copies every folder into its bundle either way.
- ../../../cockpit/assets/dungeon/sfx
knights- ../../../cockpit/assets/dungeon/sfx/knights
music- ../../../cockpit/assets/dungeon/music beside
